      "writtenOn": "2020-07-28T21:05:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggested it, pretty much for the same reason why MessageHandler and LooperCallback hold a weak_ptr to PointerController to make the ownership relation clear.\n\nTBH if MessageHandler and LooperCallback aren\u0027t holding weak_ptr, I would suggest having the basic type in PointerController and holding a reference here instead. If you think weak_ptr is an overkill, let\u0027s do this instead.",
      "parentUuid": "de45ccfa_d61fef3a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "2f07e39eca4846dc8f6da0b0c7f89850c8cdd200",
