    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "27e4130f_cf50eaf0",
        "filename": "libs/input/MouseCursorController.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 179,
      "author": {
        "id": 1109308
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-27T22:43:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t call lock() every time you need mContext. You should capture a shared_ptr of PointerControllerContext at the beginning of every function in a local variable and use that instead.\n\nlock() of a weak ptr needs a CAS operation in a while loop (more or less like a spin lock) so it can be expensive. More importantly (though not possible in this particular case), locking a weak ptr comes with pointer validity check so it could be possible that only a part of a function is executed. It\u0027s not necessary to check the validity after we lock it in this file (or if we really want we can use LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL_IF), but I still would like to see PointerControllerContext captured in a local variable before using it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 179,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 179,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "2f07e39eca4846dc8f6da0b0c7f89850c8cdd200",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
