      "writtenOn": "2020-07-27T22:43:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was hoping you could have noticed this when I was asking you not to pass PointerController.\n\nI have 2 layers of questions here.\n\nFirst layer (code layer):\nThis should just be mContext.lock()-\u003eclearSpotsLocked(). The delegating to PointerController should be detail in PointerControllerContext.\n\nSecond layer (product layer):\nWhy do we clear spots when viewport changed on earth? Isn\u0027t the viewport only for mouse cursor?\n\nThis is an example in real world that we need to answer a more abstract question before we can even think about the code. I\u0027d say we should just remove this statement, which just makes the question on the first layer invalid.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 243,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 243,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "2f07e39eca4846dc8f6da0b0c7f89850c8cdd200",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
